---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config";
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description={`${site.name} privacy policy — we don't collect or transmit your colors. Everything runs locally.`}
>
  <section class="px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="heading-section text-[36px] sm:text-[44px] mb-6 text-balance">Your colors. Your device.</h1>

      <p class="text-[18px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-10">
        <span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Short version:</span> {site.name} runs 100% in your browser.
        We don't collect, store, or transmit the colors you pick. We never see them. They never leave your device.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[20px] mb-4 mt-12">What we don't collect</h2>
      <ul class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-12 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li>The colors you pick — they're returned directly by the browser to JavaScript running on this page; the network never sees them.</li>
        <li>Your palette history — stored exclusively in your browser's <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">localStorage</code>, which we have no way to read remotely.</li>
        <li>Your IP address, beyond the standard webserver logs that every site keeps for 30 days for abuse prevention.</li>
        <li>Any account info — there are no accounts. We don't even have a sign-up form.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[20px] mb-4 mt-12">What we do measure (aggregate only)</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-4">
        To keep a free tool alive we use <span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Google Analytics 4</span> for anonymous, aggregate usage
        (page views, approximate region, device type). It sets analytics cookies and never sees the colors you pick.
        We may also show <span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Google AdSense</span> ads, which use advertising cookies.
        Both are disclosed in full — including how to opt out — in our
        <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="prose-link">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-12">
        Beyond that, the only other data anyone collects is whatever Cloudflare's CDN logs at the edge to serve the static page itself.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[20px] mb-4 mt-12">Third-party services we use</h2>
      <ul class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Cloudflare Pages</span> — hosts the static HTML/CSS/JS. <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Their privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Google Analytics 4</span> — anonymous aggregate usage measurement. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Google AdSense</span> (if ads are shown) — contextual advertising. <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">How Google uses advertising data</a>.</li>
        <li><span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Google Fonts</span> — serves the Geist font family. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Google's privacy policy</a>. We may self-host fonts in a future release to remove this dependency.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[20px] mb-4 mt-12">Your local data</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-4">
        Your palette history is saved in <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">localStorage</code> under the key <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">screencolorpicker:palette:v1</code>.
        To wipe it, click <span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] italic">"Clear all"</span> in the palette section, or clear site data via browser settings.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-12">
        Your theme preference (dark/light) is also in localStorage under <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">screencolorpicker:theme</code>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[20px] mb-4 mt-12">Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7]">
        Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="prose-link">{site.contactEmail}</a>,
        or see the full <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="prose-link">Privacy Policy</a> for your GDPR/CCPA rights and opt-out links.
      </p>

      <p class="text-[12px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-fg-subtle)] mt-16">
        Last updated: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
